+
+// The settle, the browser half: has the
+// page finished reacting to the agent's action? Each local root's renderer
+// watches its own frames (AgentSettleWatcher, through the collector's
+// ArmSettle / AwaitSettle / DisarmSettle); this joins them.
+//
+// SettleArm: one per ActionOutcomeWatch, armed at the watch's own arm (the
+// same id, T = the arm's time) or by Page.agentSettleArm. It sends
+// ArmSettle(id, T, look) to every live local root of the page -- messages
+// only, nothing waits for a renderer -- arms a local root that commits a new
+// document while armed at that commit, and keeps what only the browser sees
+// since T: the main frame's URL changes, its first cross-document commit, a
+// new tab.
+//
+// SettleJoin: one Page.agentSettle call. Every live local root of the page
+// is awaited on the pipe its arm went on (so the arm arrives first); `until`
+// is waited for first (text, selector or xpath in every local root -- with a
+// frame, only its own -- a gone element only in its own, a URL or a new tab
+// here), then the settle after it. Settled is every renderer settled and no
+// navigation pending (the watch's). A main frame that commits during it is
+// armed at the commit and the cap restarts from there, once. A renderer that
+// never answers cannot hold the call: its pipe closing answers it, and the
+// browser's own deadline ends the wait.
+
