+              array<int32> veil_node_ids) => (int32 index);
+
+  // browser: an element's slot as it is now.
+  ReadSlot(int32 node_id) => (AgentSlot slot);
+
+  // browser: what the focused field of the focused frame under this
+  // local root holds (the local root's own document's when focus is in none
+  // of its frames). With settle_ms > 0, looked at again every frame or so
+  // until the reading has held for quiet_ms -- with settle_for_text, and holds
+  // `expect` (a field too long to look in counts as holding it) -- or
+  // settle_ms has passed. before_node_id names the field a reading before the
+  // action found in this local root (0: none), for `moved`; no_typos is the
+  // rule for `strict`.
+  ReadField(int32 before_node_id, string? expect, int32 settle_ms,
+            int32 quiet_ms, bool settle_for_text, AgentNoTypos? no_typos)
+      => (AgentFieldReading? reading);
+
+  // browser: Input.fillDateTime's read of a date or time field (an
+  // input of type date, time, datetime-local, month or week, drawn with its
+  // parts): its parts in order, with their ranges, values and focus, its
+  // validity, and, with a non-empty `want`, how it would take that (judged on
+  // an input of the same kind in the document's inert template document,
+  // never the page's). Read-only: brings style and layout clean in its
+  // document.
+  ReadTemporal(int32 local_dom_node_id, string want)
+      => (AgentTemporalReading reading);
+
+  // browser: Input.pickColor's read of a colour field (an input of
+  // type color): whether it is disabled, whether it holds `want` (as it would
+  // take it), and whether its picker shows. Read-only.
+  ReadColor(int32 local_dom_node_id, string want)
+      => (AgentColorReading reading);
+
+  // browser: Input.pickColor's pick: `value` (#rrggbb) committed in the
+  // colour field's open picker through the picker's own controller, as its
+  // script commits a typed hex code that Enter closes it on: the field takes
+  // it (one trusted input, and change once the picker has closed) and the
+  // picker closes. An empty value closes it with nothing chosen, as Escape
+  // does, even one the browser has not shown yet. picked; closed (the empty
+  // value); notOpen (no picker of the field's shows); notColor; badValue
+  // (neither #rrggbb nor empty); gone.
+  CommitColor(int32 local_dom_node_id, string value) => (string outcome);
+
+  // browser: Input.chooseFiles' read of an element (AgentFileReading),
+  // with `want` the names its files should have (empty: none asked).
+  // Read-only: brings style and layout clean in its document.
+  ReadFileField(int32 local_dom_node_id, array<string> want)
+      => (AgentFileReading reading);
+
+  // browser: the file input whose chooser is open in the frame
+  // `frame_id` (its DevTools frame token) under this local root, shadow
+  // trees in, read as ReadFileField reads one; kind gone for none (a field
+  // the page made and never put in the page has none to find), unread when
+  // the page is too large to look through. Only that frame: a page queues
+  // choosers, and each one queued marks its field open. Read-only.
+  ReadOpenFileField(string frame_id) => (AgentFileReading reading);
+
+  // browser: the value a range input would take for a press or a drag at
+  // (x, y), as SliderThumbElement::SetPositionFromPoint computes it. ok is
+  // false for anything but a range input.
+  ValueAtPoint(int32 node_id, double x, double y) => (bool ok, double value);
+
+  // browser: the frame element in this local root (its same-process frames
+  // included) that holds the frame whose DevTools token is `frame_token`,
+  // and its node id; found false when none does (a reveal brings it in
+  // before what that frame holds).
+  OwnerOf(string frame_token) => (bool found, int32 node_id);
+
+  // browser: the settle. T is the action's time in the browser's TimeTicks. A
+  // new arm answers a call still waiting on the one before.
+  //
+  // browser: `look`: a settle armed by a look (Page.agentSettle with no
+  // armId), not by an action: what the regions said since the last action is
+  // kept.
+  ArmSettle(int64 arm_id, mojo_base.mojom.TimeTicks t, bool look);
+
+  // Answers when this local root has settled, the deadline passed, or `until`
+  // is met (then settles after it). quiet/cap in ms. An `until` waits until
+  // the browser's deadline (DisarmSettle or a new AwaitSettle), 60 s at most.
+  //
+  // browser: `report`: also this local root's part of the per-action
+  // report, read in a task of its own once it has settled.
+  AwaitSettle(int64 arm_id,
+              int32 quiet_ms,
+              int32 cap_ms,
+              AgentUntil? until,
+              AgentReportOptions? report)
+      => (AgentSettleReading reading);
+
+  // Ends the arm, answering a call still waiting. Also ended by the next arm
+  // or the watcher's own 10 s lease.
+  DisarmSettle(int64 arm_id);
+
+  // browser: liveness of nodes by DOMNodeId. No layout, no
+  // accessibility tree, no script.
+  NodesAlive(array<int32> node_ids) => (array<AgentNodeState> nodes);
+
+  // browser: the live regions of this local root's documents, and what
+  // they said since the last action's ArmSettle, with what that ArmSettle
+  // carried on. Forces nothing; waits at most 100 ms for a pending lifecycle.
+  LiveRegions() => (array<AgentRegionRead> regions,
+                    array<AgentHeardRead> heard);
+
+  // browser: this local root's part of the per-action report of the
+  // arm `arm_id` at once (LiveRegions' read, its closing pass included;
+  // layers when asked); `superseded`, unread, when this renderer's latest arm
+  // is another. Sent on the pipe that armed, so it comes after its ArmSettle.
+  ReportNow(int64 arm_id, AgentReportOptions options)
+      => (AgentFrameReport report);
+
+  // browser: forces a commit and holds the frame it draws still, with
+  // what it draws of text, text fields, card fields and moving boxes, so the
+  // browser can copy it and paint its secrets out; `hold` releases it. Text
+  // past `max_text_chars` is not returned. One freeze at a time.
+  FreezeForCopy(int32 max_text_chars, pending_receiver<AgentFreezeHold> hold)
+      => (AgentFreezeReply reply);
+};
